title: "CounterfactMe: Generate Random Counterfactual Lives Based on Norwegian Open Data"
authors:
  - family-names: Isungset
    given-names: Martin Arstad
    email: martinisungset@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6903-6807"
version: 0.9.35
date-released: "2026-08-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/martinisungset/CounterfactMe"
url: "https://github.com/martinisungset/CounterfactMe"
type: software
keywords:
  - sociology
  - demography
  - counterfactual
  - simulation
  - Norway
  - SSB
  - R-package
abstract: >
  CounterfactMe generates random but plausible counterfactual Norwegian
  lives from open Statistics Norway (SSB) data. Each call to
  counterfact_me() returns a coherent life across 33+ dimensions
  (name, age, education, occupation, income, family structure, housing,
  wealth, religion, party, class profile, health, hobbies, and more),
  conditionally sampled in sociologically realistic order.
